; The title tune player as the game runs it. Its bytes are encrypted in the
; snapshot, so the main listing holds them as data; the Makefile decrypts them
; (tools/tune_player.py) and disassembles them with src/tune.ctl into
; build/tune.skool. This file makes that listing the "tune" code of the site.

[OtherCode:tune]
Source=tune.skool

[MemoryMap:tune-Index]
EntryTypes=bcgw
Intro=The title tune player as the game runs it. #R$F009@main(Its bytes) are encrypted in the program image, and #R$F006@main(the routine that runs it) decrypts them before each play. The listing shows them decrypted, at the addresses they occupy.
